# toke — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local for manual local work, or generate it from Vercel:
#     npm run env:pull        (vercel env pull .env.local)
#
# .env.local is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# SECURITY: toke is entirely client-side. Every NEXT_PUBLIC_ value is inlined into
# the browser bundle at build time and is readable by anyone. No secret, key, token
# or credential may ever be placed in this file or in Vercel's env settings for this
# project. There is no server to keep one on.

# --- build metadata -------------------------------------------------------
# Surfaced in the diagnostics panel so a bug report can name an exact build.
# Vercel populates these automatically; no need to set them by hand.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA=

# --- feature flags --------------------------------------------------------
# Unreleased phases, off by default. See IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md §Non-Goals.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_SQL_CONSOLE=false
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_REPEATERS=false
